{
  "analysis": "The review describes a chance-based wheel reward mechanic in which the player appears to stop on a valuable prize, but the game then forces a reroll and replaces it with a substantially lower prize. The outcome is therefore described as being manipulated after the apparent result, supporting Illusion of Control. The wheel itself is a random reward-delivery system, supporting Reward Mania. The review does not explicitly describe spending money or wagering paid currency on the wheel, so Gambling is not assigned.",
  "labels": [
    {
      "label": "P_IllusionOfControl",
      "span": "the wheel spin after stopping on a great price the genie move the wheel to a spin tag, and then the prices after the spin are way lower than the original price",
      "rule_applied": "vs Alleged rigging",
      "rationale": "The span describes the game overriding an apparent wheel result and manipulating the reward determination to produce a lower prize."
    },
    {
      "label": "P_RewardMania",
      "span": "the wheel spin",
      "rule_applied": "Variable Rewards",
      "rationale": "The wheel is a chance-based reward-delivery mechanic whose unpredictable outcomes sustain engagement."
    }
  ],
  "invoked_web_search": false,
  "search_query": null,
  "search_result": null
}

{
  "analysis": "The review attributes the inability to open gifts, trade, catch Pokémon, and complete battles to crashing, lag, freezing, and unresponsive controls. Those technical faults do not support dark-pattern labels for the affected behaviors. The review does explicitly describe PvP, including an opponent attacking, which indicates competition as an underlying game mechanic.",
  "labels": [
    {
      "label": "S_Competition",
      "span": "the pvp & rockets battles",
      "rule_applied": "definition",
      "rationale": "PvP battles place the player against an opponent, which is competition between players."
    }
  ],
  "invoked_web_search": false,
  "search_query": null,
  "search_result": null
}

{
  "analysis": "The review describes a 30-second matchmaking connection delay, but this is a service or queue wait rather than an in-game timer that deliberately gates play, so it does not support Playing by Appointment. The reviewer also says that obtaining weapon upgrades and perks requires battling to win, which describes competitive play against other players. The claim that rewards are only for show is too vague to establish a specific reward-delivery or deceptive-interface mechanic, and the general complaint about wasted time is not itself a labelable mechanic.",
  "labels": [
    {
      "label": "S_Competition",
      "span": "battling to win",
      "rule_applied": "definition",
      "rationale": "The span describes competing in battles to win, indicating that the game makes players compete against others."
    }
  ],
  "invoked_web_search": false,
  "search_query": null,
  "search_result": null
}

{
  "analysis": "The review describes a competitive card-battling game in which the player faces other players and tries to win, so Competition applies. It explicitly characterizes the game as pay to win, meaning spending money provides an advantage or makes progression toward higher trophies easier, so Pay to Progress applies. The complaints about annoying cards and updates buffing disliked cards are balance evaluations, not evidence of power creep, rigged outcomes, or anti-social incentives.",
  "labels": [
    {
      "label": "S_Competition",
      "span": "all you play against after 8k trophies is mega knight,pekka, and golem",
      "rule_applied": "definition",
      "rationale": "The reviewer explicitly describes playing against other players using particular cards, which is competition."
    },
    {
      "label": "M_PayToProgress",
      "span": "its also pay to win",
      "rule_applied": "Pay to Win",
      "rationale": "The span explicitly states that spending money provides an advantage in winning and advancing."
    }
  ],
  "invoked_web_search": false,
  "search_query": null,
  "search_result": null
}

{
  "analysis": "The review describes a paid pass as an in-game purchase option, which supports the recurring-fee label because a pass is a battle-pass-style product. It also explicitly describes players trading lives, a resource exchange between existing players, which supports Reciprocity. The mention of 9 diamonds and additional moves does not clearly describe a timer, paid progression barrier, chance mechanic, or currency conversion. The statement that players do not have to pay to win is an evaluation of monetization and does not itself establish a dark-pattern mechanic.",
  "labels": [
    {
      "label": "M_RecurringFee",
      "span": "beyond the pass",
      "rule_applied": "Battle passes, MMO-subscriptions",
      "rationale": "The review names a pass as a paid in-game product, which is a listed recurring-fee indicator."
    },
    {
      "label": "S_Reciprocity",
      "span": "trade lives",
      "rule_applied": "definition",
      "rationale": "Players exchange lives with one another, describing a resource-trading mechanic that can create reciprocal obligations."
    }
  ],
  "invoked_web_search": false,
  "search_query": null,
  "search_result": null
}

{
  "analysis": "The review describes two existing time-based retention mechanics. First, lives are replenished on an in-game timer, as shown by the request for a new life within 5–10 minutes; the requested shorter duration implies that the current wait is longer. This is a Wait to Play mechanic. Second, the game has daily prizes that reset when the player misses a day, which is a daily reward system with a missed-day penalty. The comments about harder levels and celebrating tasks are evaluations or suggestions without enough detail to support additional labels.",
  "labels": [
    {
      "label": "T_PlayingByAppointment",
      "span": "maybe only 5-10 minutes for a new life",
      "rule_applied": "Wait to Play",
      "rationale": "The request for a new life within 5–10 minutes implies that lives currently regenerate on an in-game timer, making continued play depend on the game's schedule."
    },
    {
      "label": "T_DailyRewards",
      "span": "just because you miss a day doesnt mean that you need to start over on your daily prizes",
      "rule_applied": "Daily log-in reward calendars; encourages return visits every day and punishes you for missing a day",
      "rationale": "Daily prizes reset when the player misses a day, which is an incentive for daily return with an explicit missed-day penalty."
    }
  ],
  "invoked_web_search": false,
  "search_query": null,
  "search_result": null
}

{
  "analysis": "The review describes an in-game advertisement that cannot be dismissed normally. The player is forced to remain on the ad screen because there is no close control, and tapping the screen redirects them to the store instead of returning them to gameplay. The player must terminate the game to escape, but no progress loss or other forfeiture is described, so Mandatory Marathon does not apply.",
  "labels": [
    {
      "label": "T_Advertisement",
      "span": "after seeing the ads, there is no way to close it",
      "rule_applied": "definition",
      "rationale": "The advertisement blocks normal play and cannot be dismissed, compelling the player to view it."
    },
    {
      "label": "M_UIMisdirection",
      "span": "No cross mark on the screen , if you try to click anywhere on the screen it takes you to store",
      "rule_applied": "vs Attention-directing without an opt-out",
      "rationale": "The interface removes the normal opt-out and routes taps toward the store instead of providing a way to close the advertisement."
    }
  ],
  "invoked_web_search": false,
  "search_query": null,
  "search_result": null
}

{
  "analysis": "The review describes empire-building and expansion, which are ordinary strategy-game mechanics and do not match a dark-pattern label. It also explicitly describes real-time battles against other players, establishing player-versus-player competition. The positive evaluation, graphics, storyline, and strategic depth do not independently support any other label.",
  "labels": [
    {
      "label": "S_Competition",
      "span": "the thrill of battling other players in real-time combat",
      "rule_applied": "definition",
      "rationale": "The game makes players compete directly against other players in real-time combat."
    }
  ],
