{
  "analysis": "The reviewer describes a very high level and slow advancement, but a high level and long time per level do not by themselves establish Grinding or Infinite Treadmill. Running out of lives several times daily describes resource depletion, but no refill timer or waiting schedule is stated, so it does not establish Playing by Appointment. The explicit mechanic is that buying add-ons is necessary to get through the levels; the unpaid route is described as unworkable, which is Pay to Progress. The reviewer says they are uninstalling despite wasted time and money, so the text does not show accumulated investment making it difficult to leave and does not support Easy to Get, Hard to Lose.",
  "labels": [
    {
      "label": "M_PayToProgress",
      "span": "You must buy add ons else you can't make it through a sane mind. it's pure time waste if you're not paying.",
      "rule_applied": "Pay Wall; vs Free alternative",
      "rationale": "The reviewer states that continued or workable progress requires buying add-ons, while the unpaid route is excessively difficult and time-consuming."
    }
  ],
  "invoked_web_search": false,
  "search_query": null,
  "search_result": null
}

{
